# Response headers for Cloudflare's static-asset server. Every rule whose
# pattern matches is applied, so the /_astro/* immutable Cache-Control rule the
# Cloudflare adapter appends at build time sits alongside this one rather than
# replacing it. Copied verbatim into dist/client/ by the build.
#
# No Strict-Transport-Security here: HSTS is Cloudflare's own setting, on the
# zone, and setting it twice invites the two to disagree.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy, term by term:
#   default-src 'self'        everything not named below comes from this origin
#   img-src 'self' data:      site images; data: for any inlined SVG or favicon
#   style-src 'unsafe-inline' the build inlines every stylesheet into the page
#                             (build.inlineStylesheets: 'always'), and Astro
#                             component styles are inline by nature
#   script-src                Turnstile's api.js, plus two inline scripts by hash:
#                             the one on /contact/ (topic preselect, and the
#                             contact form submitted with fetch) and the one on
#                             the workshop page (copy buttons, seats left read
#                             from /api/seats/, the laptop fields hidden while
#                             the watch-only box is ticked, and the registration
#                             form submitted with fetch)
#                             (npm run check:csp)
#   frame-src, connect-src    the Turnstile widget's iframe and its callbacks;
#                             connect-src also takes Cloudflare Web Analytics,
#                             whose beacon the zone injects into every page
#                             (script-src allows static.cloudflareinsights.com)
#   base-uri, form-action     no injected <base>, no cross-origin form posts;
#                             both forms post to /api/ on this origin
#   frame-ancestors 'none'    the site is never framed
#
# Each sha256 covers one page's script in src/pages/ exactly as Astro emits it,
# whitespace and indentation included, so reindenting a block changes its hash.
# `npm run check:csp` recomputes the hashes from the built HTML and fails if
# this file has fallen behind. The JSON-LD blocks need no hash:
# type="application/ld+json" is data, not script, and the policy does not apply
# to it.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; script-src 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com 'sha256-/C/7qyOpMgiGka/X5t8A0RErUfPCdk5lgkcD1Rv8XME=' 'sha256-KQmpuos6a2ww4i8HpvOVQGiI2oMakCwkuVTylV1lGNc='; frame-src https://challenges.cloudflare.com; connect-src 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://cloudflareinsights.com; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
